  "executiveChampionReason": "Sean, Tom and Rossane are the VPs of Cloud Solutioning Center covering the three centers West, East and US respectively. They are responsible for solutioning high value deals based on OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks. They want to ensure optimal and standard solutions for OpenShift across all the markets.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Kyle is an IBM Fellow for IBM Cloud Garage and Solution Engineering. He needs to make sure the right guidance about OpenShift and Cloud Paks are transferred to the broad IBMers.",
  "associatedBusinessUnit": "",
  "associatedBusinessUnitOther": "",
  "focusArea": "Hybrid Multicloud",
  "affiliateName": [],
  "startDate": { "$date": "2020-09-11T00:00:00.000Z" },
  "endDate": { "$date": "2021-04-27T00:00:00.000Z" },
  "description": "Update the deliverables from the AoT initiative (Red Hat OpenShift - Solution Design Guidance), make sure that the guides are effective, and publish suitable content of the guides externally including Architecture Center.",
  "problemStatement": "Need published guidance on how to design optimal OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks solutions for our clients, ensure architectural integrity, and proper delivery structure using the 14-in-4 offerings.\r\n\r\nThe first version of 5 (five) Solution Design Guidance for OpenShift were published as part of the AoT Initiative: Red Hat OpenShift - Solution Design Guidance: https://w3.ibm.com/ibm/academy/ecard/a7f9863a166805f498ca962e06fe38ab\r\n\r\nSince OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks content are evolving rapidly, need to work on Red Hat OpenShift - Solution Design Guidance 2.0 to address the following:\r\n1) Maintain the 5 guides \r\n2) Make sure that guides are effective and leveraged across brands to design optimal OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks solutions\r\n3) Publish suitable content of the guides externally on IBM Cloud Architecture Center.\r\n4) Work with Red Hat to enhance the quality of the guides",
  "outcome": "**Expected Outcome:**\r\n1- Update the 5 guides produced as part of the earlier AoT initiative and publish on https://ibm.biz/openshift-solutioning\r\nA) OpenShift Solutioning Guide 101\r\nB) Cloud Paks Guidance\r\nC) OpenShift Resilience Guidance\r\nD) OpenShift Architecture Patterns\r\nE) OpenShift Solution Clinic Report\r\n2- Publish suitable content of the guides externally on IBM Cloud Architecture Center.\r\n\r\n**Business Value**\r\nA) Standardize and optimize OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks solutions to our customers by having all the technical communities following the approach identified in the above five guides.\r\nB) Validate the technical accuracy of the guides with broader technical experts cross business unit to assure we are delivering optimal OpenShift and IBM Cloud Paks solutions to our customers.\r\nC) The guides will be leveraged across Cloud & Cognitive Software, GTS, and GBS as well as the wider IBM - to design optimal OpenShift solutions for our clients. This fulfills the need to ensure architectural integrity and proper delivery structure in our solutions which will result in better business outcomes for our clients and IBM.\r\n",
  "finalOutcome": "",
